{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794326766,"nonce":"28pfXJ+Noun06BfHjbB+EaC9ed0=","message":"Owner direction: Apple targets go to a native Metal backend (310506c) that takes russl's MSL directly, so wgpu's Metal passthrough gap does not matter. Remaining for bypassing naga through wgpu: Windows D3D12 and WebGL2. Notes: (1) wgpu's WebGPU backend already hands WGSL to the browser, so naga is not in that runtime path; only its GLES backend uses naga on the web. (2) Vulkan SPIR-V passthrough works in wgpu 26, so Windows could run Vulkan with the same SPIR-V as Android and Linux, which avoids a separate D3D12 artifact path; the alternative is HLSL/DXIL passthrough with one module per stage, unverified for render, or a native D3D12 backend behind c546365. (3) WebGL2 has no passthrough in wgpu; bypassing naga there means GLSL ES through our own WebGL2 backend (4477494), or accepting naga on that one path. The russl sources are needed for every route, so the port order does not change.","files":null}]}